  "published": "2026-10-13T05:12:40.607Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "DotCov 3.0.0 changes three gate contracts; every number a gate decides on may move.\n1. Thresholds are explicit: check, test, the Fallout target and the badge action have no default --min-line 80. Pass --min-line, --min-branch, or both (0 to 100); without either the command exits 2 before reading a report.\n2. The CRAP gate needs every method scored: one unscored method makes it NODATA (exit 3). Emitters without a usable complexity attribute need --metrics.\n3. File identity is deterministic: several source roots no longer trigger a disk probe; unresolved files make check, crap and test NODATA until --probe-sources or --source-root.\nFixes: contradictory condition detail and empty class summaries no longer inflate branch and line rates; condition identity no longer depends on XML packaging; CRAP rows stay per file and per overload, raising diluted scores; ./src/C.cs and src/C.cs count once; ParseAsync finishes method-only classes.\nNew: --exclude-test-code. Full notes: https://github.com/ANcpLua/dotcov/blob/main/docs/releases/3.0.0.md",
